/-!
# Completion criterion for local complete intersections

Source: Stacks Project, dpa.tex, Tags 09Q1, 09Q3, 09Q6, and Algebra Tags 00SG, 00SB
(blueprint: lem-trf-completion-local-complete-intersection).

## Main statements

* `completion_local_complete_intersection_iff`: a finite type algebra is locally a
  complete intersection at a maximal ideal exactly when its completed local ring is a
  power-series quotient by a regular sequence; the local ring is then Cohen--Macaulay.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace Algebra

/-- (blueprint: lem-trf-completion-local-complete-intersection) Stacks Project, dpa.tex,
Tags 09Q1, 09Q3 and 09Q6, together with Algebra Tags 00SG and 00SB. The completed local
ring criterion for a local complete intersection and the resulting depth equality.

Proof (blueprint steps).

1. (dpa 09Q6; Algebra 0316, 05GI, 05GG) Choose a surjection `P = k[x_1, …, x_n] → S`
   (def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra) with kernel `I`, and let `𝔮` be the inverse image of
   `𝔭`. By lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-field-regular-ring, `R = P_𝔮` is regular local,
   hence Noetherian. The map `R / IR → A`, `(u/v) mod IR ↦ ū/v̄`, is an isomorphism, so
   lem-weil-pbc-surjective-image-noetherian makes `A` Noetherian. Put `C = Â`. By
   lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-noetherian and lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-local-ring,
   `C` is Noetherian local with maximal ideal `𝔫 = 𝔭AC` and residue field `F`; by
   lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-mod-ideal it is `𝔫`-adically complete.
2. (Algebra 032A (1), 0326) `C` contains the field `k`, so `C` and `F` have the same
   characteristic `p`. By lem-weil-pbc-cohen-coefficient-ring-exists, `C` has a coefficient
   ring `Λ` with maximal ideal `pΛ = 0`; so `Λ` is a field and the residue isomorphism gives
   a ring map `α : F → C` whose composite with `C → F` is the identity (not necessarily
   `k`-linear; the conclusion is an isomorphism of rings).
3. (Algebra 032A, 032C, 0315) Choose generators `y_1, …, y_r` of `𝔫`
   (def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring) and set `Q = F[[z_1, …, z_r]]`, complete regular local
   with maximal ideal `𝔩 = (z_1, …, z_r)` (lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-regular-
   complete). lem-weil-pbc-power-series-universal-property-complete gives
   `ψ : Q → C`, `z_i ↦ y_i`, extending `α`. Then `𝔩C = 𝔫`, `Q → C/𝔫 = F` is surjective,
   so lem-weil-pbc-complete-source-surjective-mod-ideal makes `ψ` surjective; its kernel
   lies in `𝔩` since series outside `𝔩` are units.
4. (dpa 09Q0, 09Q1, 09PZ; Algebra 00SB) Assume (1). By def-weil-pbc-complete-intersection-
   over-field the prime of `S_g` given by `𝔭` lies in some `D(a)` with `T = (S_g)_a` a
   nonzero global complete intersection `k[w_1, …, w_m]/(f_1, …, f_t)`, `dim T = m - t`.
   With `R_T` the localization of the polynomial ring at our point (regular local by
   lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-field-regular-ring), the `f_i` form a regular sequence in
   `R_T` (lem-weil-pbc-global-complete-intersection-local-regular-sequence), and
   `A ≅ R_T/(f_1, …, f_t)`. lem-trf-regular-quotient-completion-kernel-test, applied to this
   quotient and to `ψ`, makes `ker ψ` generated by a regular sequence `h_1, …, h_c` in
   `𝔩`, and `Q/(h_1, …, h_c) ≅ C` as rings. This is (2).
5. (dpa 09Q1; Algebra 00SC (5) ⇒ (1), 00SG) Assume (2). `Q_0 = F[[z_1, …, z_r]]` is regular
   local (lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-regular-complete); composing its quotient
   map with the given isomorphism is a surjection `Q_0 → C` with kernel generated by the
   regular sequence `(h_i)`. lem-trf-regular-quotient-completion-kernel-test, applied to
   `R = P_𝔮` and `IR` of step 1, gives a regular sequence generating `IR`; then
   lem-weil-pbc-lci-regular-sequence-global-complete-intersection gives `g ∉ 𝔭` with `S_g`
   a global complete intersection, hence a local complete intersection with the single
   cover `D(1)` (def-weil-pbc-complete-intersection-over-field). This is (1).
6. (Algebra 00SB, 00NQ, 02JN, 00LK) Under these conditions take `A ≅ R_T/(f_1, …, f_t)` from
   step 4. `R_T` has finite dimension `d` (lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-local-finite-krull-
   dimension); `d` generators of its maximal ideal (def-weil-regular-scheme) form a regular
   sequence (lem-weil-pbc-regular-local-generators-regular-sequence), so
   `depth R_T ≥ d` (def-weil-pbc-depth). By induction on `i`, `R_i = R_T/(f_1, …, f_i)` is
   Noetherian local with `depth R_i ≥ dim R_i`, by
   lem-weil-pbc-cm-local-quotient-nonzerodivisor-cm since `f_{i+1}` is a nonzerodivisor on
   `R_i` in its maximal ideal. Hence `depth A ≥ dim A`; the reverse inequality is
   lem-weil-pbc-depth-le-support-dimension for the module `A`, whose support is
   `Spec A`. If `S` is a local complete intersection, (1) holds at every maximal ideal with
   `g = 1`, which gives the last clause. -/
theorem completion_local_complete_intersection_iff
    (k : Type u) (S : Type v) [Field k] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]
    [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (p : Ideal S) [p.IsMaximal] :
    ((∃ g : S, g ∉ p ∧ IsLocalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g)) ↔
      (∃ (r c : ℕ) (h : Fin c → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (S ⧸ p)),
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (S ⧸ p)) (List.ofFn h) ∧
          (∀ i : Fin c,
            h i ∈ Ideal.span
              (Set.range (fun j : Fin r => MvPowerSeries.X j))) ∧
          Nonempty
            ((MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (S ⧸ p) ⧸
                Ideal.span (Set.range h)) ≃+*
              AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p))
                (Localization.AtPrime p)))) ∧
      ((∃ g : S, g ∉ p ∧ IsLocalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g)) →
        (↑(IsLocalRing.depth (R := Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime p)) :
          WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime p)) ∧
      (IsLocalCompleteIntersection k S →
        ∀ (q : Ideal S) [hq : q.IsMaximal],
          (↑(IsLocalRing.depth (R := Localization.AtPrime q) (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
            WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q)) := by
  sorry


end Algebra
